<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="{{ app.request.locale|default('fr') }}">
    <head>
        <meta charset="UTF-8">
        <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
        <title>{% block title %}Benevolio{% endblock %}</title>
        {#
            No page is indexed unless it says so: a page that should be found sets
            `indexable` to true at its top (the home page, the guides). Forms, logins and
            links that are credentials stay out of search results without anyone having to
            remember them. See AGENTS.md, *SEO & GEO*.
        #}
        {% if not (indexable ?? false) %}
            <meta name="robots" content="noindex">
        {% endif %}
        {% block meta %}{% endblock %}
        {# The icons crawlers and browsers ask for at the root are files in public/; the
           vector one comes from AssetMapper. #}
        <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="32x32">
        <link rel="icon" href="{{ asset('images/brand/mark.svg') }}" type="image/svg+xml">
        <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/apple-touch-icon.png">
        <link rel="manifest" href="/site.webmanifest">
        <meta name="theme-color" content="#f7f4ee" media="(prefers-color-scheme: light)">
        <meta name="theme-color" content="#14191f" media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)">
        {#
            Linked here, not imported from app.js. An `import './styles/app.css'` in
            JavaScript makes AssetMapper map the file to a `data:` module in the import
            map, and a script policy would then have to allow `data:` scripts — which
            is allowing any injected <script src="data:…">, the thing the policy is for.
        #}
        {% block stylesheets %}
            <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ asset('styles/app.css') }}">
        {% endblock %}

        {#
            The one inline script in this project, and it has to be inline and here.
            The chosen theme lives in localStorage, so only JavaScript can know it —
            and anything deferred or module-loaded runs after first paint, which
            means a visitor who chose dark gets a white flash on every single page.
            Reading one key and setting one attribute is cheap enough to do before
            the browser draws anything.

            Absent or "auto" leaves no attribute, so the media query in app.css
            decides — which is also what a visitor with JavaScript off gets.

            EVERY <script> below carries csp_nonce(): these pages are served with a
            script policy (App\Security\ContentSecurityPolicyListener), and a script
            without the nonce simply does not run — silently, apart from the console.
        #}
        <script nonce="{{ csp_nonce() }}">
            try {
                var theme = localStorage.getItem('benevolio-theme');
                if (theme === 'dark' || theme === 'light') {
                    document.documentElement.dataset.theme = theme;
                }
            } catch (e) {
                // Storage can throw outright when cookies are blocked. The page
                // still works; it just follows the operating system.
            }
        </script>

        {% block javascripts %}
            {% block importmap %}{{ importmap('app', {nonce: csp_nonce()}) }}{% endblock %}
        {% endblock %}

        {% set frankenphp_hot_reload = app.request.server.get('FRANKENPHP_HOT_RELOAD') %}
        {% if frankenphp_hot_reload %}
            <meta name="frankenphp-hot-reload:url" content="{{ frankenphp_hot_reload }}">
            <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/idiomorph" nonce="{{ csp_nonce() }}"></script>
            <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/frankenphp-hot-reload/+esm" type="module" nonce="{{ csp_nonce() }}"></script>
        {% endif %}
    </head>
    <body>
        {% block body %}{% endblock %}
    </body>
</html>
